answer:
File handling in PHP allows manipulating files directly on the server:

1. Opening a file: fopen("test.txt", "w");
2. Writing to a file: fwrite($fileHandle, $data);
3. Reading from a file:
- fread($fileHandle, filesize("test.txt"))
- fgets($fileHandle) reads line-by-line
4. Closing a file: fclose($fileHandle);

Complete Working Example:
<?php
$file = fopen("sample.txt", "w");
fwrite($file, "Learning PHP File Handling.\n");
fclose($file);

$file = fopen("sample.txt", "r");
echo fread($file, filesize("sample.txt"));
fclose($file);
?>

